          "title": "You'll want to know: кипятить",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "кипятить (kipyatít) — \"to bring to the boil, to boil\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Бабушка кипятит молоко. Bábushka kipyatít molokó. Grandma is boiling milk."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective вскипятить (vskipyatít), кипячу. Кипяток — boiling water."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "кипятить (kipyatít) is built on кипеть (kipét) \"to boil\", inherited from Proto-Slavic kypěti (EtymDB): to make something boil."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
